Band Description
Indigo Brake Choir is a five-member acoustic-electronic ensemble built around two simultaneous perceptions of tempo.

Awa Sarr — xalam, slow ostinati, modal cells, muted ghost plucks, resonator-skin performance.
Theo Mercer — autonomic drum-and-bass programming, sampler, sub architecture, break editing.
Mamadou Kane — tama, pitch-bent rhythmic calls, slow/fast pulse mediation.
Elise Moreau — prepared vibraphone, sustained harmonic memory, selective damping.
Idris Cole — contrabass clarinet, low-mid apparitions, breath tones, sparse multiphonics.

There is no conventional frontperson. Awa establishes the slow perceived clock, Theo maintains the fast machine clock, Mamadou moves between them, Elise stretches harmony across both, and Idris occupies the low spaces where neither clock feels dominant. Live versions vary because the xalam and tama can shift between half- and quarter-speed implication without changing BPM.

